    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "finding": "Mean retries of 3.1/request co-occurs with the latency regression, making retry amplification a live causal candidate requiring intervention evidence.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "fixture:O1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "finding": "With pool reuse still enabled, explicit request-boundary retry-state reset reduced mean retries from 3.1/request to 1 and produced p95 latency of 219 ms versus the 412 ms baseline, strongly supporting H_retry_state as the primary causal mechanism rather than mere concurrency load relief.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "fixture:O1",
        "fixture:E_force_retry_reset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "finding": "Disabling connection-pool reuse while holding concurrency and retry policy fixed reduced mean retries from the 3.1/request baseline to 1.1 and p95 latency from 412 ms to 228 ms. This converges with the prior request-boundary retry-reset intervention (1 retry, 219 ms), supporting pooled lifecycle reuse as necessary for retry-state amplification.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "fixture:O1",
        "fixture:E_force_retry_reset",
        "fixture:E_disable_pool_reuse"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "finding": "The two discriminating interventions normalize retries and latency without reducing concurrency: explicit retry-state reset with pool reuse enabled and disabling pool reuse with retry policy fixed. This rejects queue-capacity saturation as the primary mechanism and makes O2's improvement under halved concurrency load-relief evidence rather than causal identification.",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "fixture:O1",
        "fixture:O2",
        "fixture:O3",
        "fixture:E_force_retry_reset",
        "fixture:E_disable_pool_reuse"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F7",
      "finding": "Increasing queue capacity 4x left the regression essentially intact: p95 latency was 405 ms and mean retries were 3/request versus the 412 ms, 3.1-retry baseline. Queue capacity therefore fails a direct discriminating intervention, strengthening rejection of H_queue as the primary mechanism and reinforcing pooled retry-state amplification as the causal explanation.",
